NAME

ulibFileExists - Determines whether a shared lock could be obtained on a file


SYNOPSIS

UBYTE ulibFileExists(UBYTE *FileToOpen)
                            a0


DESCRIPTION

This function attempts to obtain a shared lock on the file provided.  If it
is successful, the lock is removed.

This function can be used to see if a file exists, although it is possible
that the file did exist, but it was not possible to obtain a lock.


NOTES

This function is generally not too useful to door programmers; it was
previously used by Xenolink to check if a file needed to be created, or if an
existing file could simply be appended to.

Xenolink now uses MODE_READWRITE, which can be used to append to an existing
file, or create a file if it does not already exist.


RETURNS

0 - Was unable to obtain a shared lock
1 - Was able to obtain a shared lock (which has now been released)
